there have been many very good and some  less than great versions of the joker  but whenever people discuss potential  casting for batman's iconic nemesis you  can be fairly sure that willem defoe's  name is mentioned the foe was actually  in consideration to play the joker and  tim burton's batman and although the  role has eluded him over the years his  instantly recognizable features and  particular strengths as an actor still  make him seem like an obvious choice for  the role sure defoe is now in his 60s  and as such it might be challenging for  him to portray a supervillain spider-man  no way home of course thoroughly  debunked that idea in 2021 in that movie  defoe handedly reprises his terrifying  role as norman green goblin osbourne  who's just as off-kilter as the joker  but far more physically intimidating  what's more defoe's one condition to  revisit the role was that he'd be  allowed to do his own fight scenes as  anyone who's seen him gleefully  manhandle spider-man can attest the  actor still clearly has what it takes to  bring both the drama and the physical  presence and any super villain role he  chooses to play and as far as the  joker's requisite creepy laughter goes  the foe once again shows in no way home  that there are few who can match him on  that front  is it any wonder then that people are  once again boarding the defoe joker hype  train in fact one artist has even  created an image that shows just how  creepily effective willem defoe could be  as the joker  in this image by digital artist el  illusionista it's evident just how  easily willem dafoe could slip into the  role of joker the picture shows a  jokerfied version of dafoe with all the  classic aspects of the character green  hair red lips pale skin a wild grin and  a fashion sense that skews toward the  color purple it's clear that the joker  in the image is in the middle of  something since he has a spattering of  blood or perhaps red makeup in the  corner of his mouth then a fresh cut on  his forehead judging by the character's  fixed gaze and the snowy cityscape  visible in the background it wouldn't be  outside the realm of reason to assume  that he's locked in a rooftop showdown  with the dark knight himself all in all  this is a very impressive joker what  makes the image even more astonishing is  the fact that it's surprisingly close to  what defoe looks like in his everyday  life color pattern notwithstanding as  the last image of the artist's post  reveals the image of the foe as the  joker is based on a photo of the actor  laughing while the colors in the  background have been changed to fit the  joker theme it's clear that defoe's  features are the same in both photos  right down to the hairstyle and the  configuration of the lines on his face  even with the knowledge that defoe is  uniquely suited to play the villain it's  almost shocking to see just how casually  he can contort his face into a joker  worthy grin  the dafoe for joker fan casting has been  going on for quite a while and in a  january 2022 interview with gq defoe  noted that he's very familiar with it in  fact people have been nudging him about  the whole joker thing for years this it  appears has piqued the actor's  imagination and he's come up with at  least one possible scenario for tackling  the iconic role though as is so often  the case with the roles defoe picks it  come with a twist he told gq  there is something interesting about  like if there was a joker imposter so it  would be possible to have not dueling  jokers but someone that claims to be the  joker that isn't the joker defoe also  revealed his ideal dance partner for  such a movie and it's none other than  joaquin phoenix the star of todd  phillips joker defoe said and that kind  of opens up the possibility of an  interesting story particularly if you  had joaquin phoenix's joker and then you  had someone who is either imitating or  ripping off what he did i fantasized  about that but other than that i'm not  talking to anybody about it you're the  first one defoe of course was quick to  pump the brakes after sharing his vision  and he probably wouldn't discuss such a  project if it was actually in the works  what  still the idea of defoe's fake joker  going up against phoenix's version of  the real one is indeed intriguing after  all considering that phoenix won the  best actor oscar for his role in joker  why wouldn't a potential sequel double  down with not one but two academy  award-worthy jokers  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

